 - VERIFICATION: Six focused fake-only Swift suites passed 53 tests. The real coordinator boundary rejects every invalid profile class before injected Keychain/network fakes; all nine `SSHHostKeyDecision` cases traverse the candidate-neutral transport seam with `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication` only on accepted paths. One independently owned lifecycle registry retains concrete task, connection, observer, and callback tokens across all 16 bounded iterations; gated cancellation observes all four non-zero, and balanced teardown restores the same registry baseline after success, every rejecting host decision, an injected thrown policy, and cancellation without assigning counters to zero. Three additional cleanup/redaction matrix repetitions passed; captured-log prohibited-data, test-source live-Security, public-fixture, live-network, and self-reset-counter scans returned no matches. Coverage reported 87.75% affected lines and 87.04% affected functions; strict Swift format, core boundaries, and diff checks exited 0. The first focused compile exited 1 on a missing explicit `return`; the corrected rerun and every subsequent gate exited 0. No real Keychain, SSH connection, NetworkExtension runtime, VPN configuration, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.
+### 2026-08-30 — Sparkle key evidence exposes a pre-C1 provenance mismatch (TASK-260717-ziprhs)
