 - VERIFICATION: Six focused fake-only Swift suites passed 53 tests. The real coordinator boundary rejects every invalid profile class before injected Keychain/network fakes; all nine `SSHHostKeyDecision` cases traverse the candidate-neutral transport seam with `hostPolicy -> credentialLookup -> authentication` only on accepted paths. One independently owned lifecycle registry retains concrete task, connection, observer, and callback tokens across all 16 bounded iterations; gated cancellation observes all four non-zero, and balanced teardown restores the same registry baseline after success, every rejecting host decision, an injected thrown policy, and cancellation without assigning counters to zero. Three additional cleanup/redaction matrix repetitions passed; captured-log prohibited-data, test-source live-Security, public-fixture, live-network, and self-reset-counter scans returned no matches. Coverage reported 87.75% affected lines and 87.04% affected functions; strict Swift format, core boundaries, and diff checks exited 0. The first focused compile exited 1 on a missing explicit `return`; the corrected rerun and every subsequent gate exited 0. No real Keychain, SSH connection, NetworkExtension runtime, VPN configuration, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter operation ran.
+### 2026-08-30 — Sparkle key evidence exposes a pre-C1 provenance mismatch (TASK-260717-ziprhs)
+- EVIDENCE: The Sparkle `ed25519` item is present in the login Keychain; public metadata yields `SUPublicEDKey` `tx8SLAmqME/ldUthxRV5PFQiUt1MX65blT29cA8My1U=` and decoded-key SHA-256 fingerprint `1e9eb93b4aa611f2ebf968ee67dfa4e99f4b93ca7a7c45f76cafc4b47bf36b54`. The official Sparkle 2.9.4 archive digest matches the GitHub release digest and tag commit `b6496a74a087257ef5e6da1c5b29a447a60f5bd7`.
+- ANOMALY: Keychain creation metadata is `2026-07-05T02:04:52Z`, while Ceremony C1 began on 2026-07-28. Sparkle 2.9.4 reuses an existing key rather than overwriting it, so current evidence confirms existence/custody but cannot attest that C1 generated this key. Owner input must either accept intentional C1 adoption of the pre-existing key or reopen C1 for controlled replacement; no key material was regenerated, exported, or moved.
+- BOUNDARY: `SUPublicEDKey` pinning, CI binding, and payload/appcast sign/verify remain open under `TASK-260728-3bj9bk`. Its rotation proof must account for the project's signed-feed failure expiration of `0`, which disables Sparkle's documented lost-key feed fallback.
+- PRIVACY INCIDENT: The post-outcome scan read every Git-scoped repository file, authoritative board resource, run log, and two shell-history files without read errors. Repository, board, and run-log candidate counts were zero, but shell history contains one real Sparkle `generate_keys -x` private-export reference dated 2026-07-09 and one untimed non-redacted App Store Connect private-key filename reference; sensitive arguments and names are not reproduced. The scan correctly exited `2`. Spotlight found no indexed current Sparkle-export filename, while a bounded exhaustive home walk was stopped at exit `130`, so current disk presence remains unknown rather than absent. This contradicts C1's prior clean-history attestation and requires owner-authorized history remediation plus custody reconciliation before review handoff.

